Reason:
The extension-loader correction changes only two bundled JavaScript resources. Rebuilding the Windows CEF application for every hypothesis costs about one hour and obscures diagnosis. A diagnostic-only boundary now reuses a previously built installer, installs it in the normal isolated profile, overlays exactly loader.mjs and module-loader.mjs from the reviewed checkout, and runs the real packaged CEF journey. It is explicitly not packaging proof; a fresh installer remains required once after the behavior is green.

Safety and scope:
- Manual workflow target only, with a validated numeric source run id.
- GitHub Actions read permission is explicit.
- Only two fixed filenames are copied. Source root, regular-file type, symlink status and 64 KiB per-file bound are validated before launch.
- Any preparation or overlay error fails closed and triggers normal isolated installation cleanup.
- The diagnostic artifact remains bounded and retained for 14 days.

